  "name": "read-surface-slo-cheap-local-and-lab",
  "reason": "First recorded latency comparison for the cheap-local and lab read-surface SLO lanes (polylogue-dpm6o AC3). Command: devtools bench slo --include-lab --json, 2026-09-21, 24-core free-threaded CPython 3.14.4 workstation, 283 s benchmark phase through the managed pytest slot. 11 lanes within budget; 5 over, all gate:informational. The three lanes dpm6o names: daemon_concurrent_reads PASSES at p50 122.19 ms against 250; cli_status_cold measures p50 2745.09 / p95 3173.27 ms against an aspirational 500/800, still dominated by the import tax polylogue-8s70 owns; daemon_warm_status measures 3288.8 ms against 400/800 but at rounds=1, so its p95 is one observation, not a percentile. Also over: daemon_mixed_load 3552.66/250 (rounds=1), ingest_to_searchable 8596.35 ms/5000 (rounds=1), daemon_status_operation 112.7 ms/100 (cheap-local, 7 rounds). Measured on a shared workstation with other pytest jobs in the same pool, so these are upper bounds, not a quiet-host floor. Explained-not-ratcheted: a re-run on a quiet host is expected to move every number and records why.",
  "supersedes": null
